  <section>
    <h2 class="slate">Plans, credits and billing</h2>
    <p>AgentShot is free to use with your own model keys. Signing in gives you an AgentShot account; an AgentShot plan (Pro or Max, billed monthly or yearly) or a one-time top-up adds credits that pay for models, voice and music through AgentShot’s gateway. Your account, plan and credits are shared with Pitch (trypitch.co): it is one account and one balance in both apps.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Payment.</strong> Prices are in US dollars, plus any tax shown at checkout. Payments are processed by Dodo Payments, which acts as merchant of record and its terms apply to the payment.</li>
      <li><strong>Renewal.</strong> Plans renew automatically at the start of each billing period until you cancel. You can cancel any time in AgentShot under Settings → Keys → AgentShot key → Manage billing; the plan, its model tiers and its credits stay until the end of the period you paid for, and it does not renew.</li>
      <li><strong>Credits.</strong> A plan grants its credits at the start of each period (a yearly plan grants the whole year’s at once); top-ups grant theirs when paid. Credits you were granted don’t expire while your account exists, even after a plan ends. Credits have no cash value and can’t be transferred, sold or exchanged. Starter credits and promotional credits may be changed or withdrawn.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage.</strong> Credits are used as you use models, voice and music with the AgentShot key; the app shows your balance. Usage prices, including launch discounts, may change; we’ll show current pricing in the app and on agentshot.si, and changes apply to usage after they take effect.</li>
      <li><strong>Price changes.</strong> If a plan’s price changes, we’ll tell you at least 30 days ahead, and the new price applies from your next renewal. You can cancel before then.</li>
      <li><strong>Failed payments.</strong> If a renewal can’t be charged, the plan is put on hold and ends if payment doesn’t go through; credits already granted stay in your balance.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
